course: dictionary
lesson: 11102
title: Wherever you go
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wherever is a small word with a big job. It can mean "in any place": «Sit wherever you like.» You get to choose the place, so any seat is fine.
explain: It can also mean "no matter where": «Wherever you go, I will find you.» The place does not change the result. Read the whole sentence to see which meaning fits.
explain: In a question, wherever shows surprise: «Wherever did you find that?» The speaker is amazed. Try the swap test: put "in any place" or "no matter where" into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Wherever means in any place, or in every place.
fact: «Wherever possible» means whenever you can.
fact: «Wherever there is light and water, plants can grow.» Plants grow in every place that has light and water.
fact: Wherever can link two parts of a sentence, as in «Wherever she goes, her dog follows.»
fact: In a question, «wherever» shows surprise, as in «Wherever did you find that?»
exercise: «Sit wherever you like.» In this sentence, wherever means | *In any place you choose | Only at the back of the room | Before you have eaten | At the wrong time
exercise: «Wherever you go, I will find you.» What does wherever mean? | Very fast | *No matter where | In a question, showing surprise | In no place at all
exercise: Which sentence shows surprise? | «Wherever you go, I will find you.» | *«Wherever did you find that?» | «Sit wherever you like.»
test: Which phrase means "whenever you can"? | *wherever possible | or wherever | wherever she goes | wherever you like
test: «Wherever she goes, her dog follows.» What does wherever mean? | Quickly and quietly | In a question, showing surprise | *No matter where she goes | Only in the house
exam: Which meaning fits «Put the bag wherever there is room»? | Lost forever | Only at the bottom of the stairs | In a question, showing surprise | *In any place that has room
